[-] cozy		<-->	a++[--0]	./ˈkəʊzi/NAmE /ˈkəʊzi/ (North American English) (British English cosy) (cozier, coziest, cosier, cosiest)
	;ấm cúng, thân mật -- (1) warm, comfortable and safe, especially in a small space
		;synonym snug
		;a cozy little room
		;a cozy feeling
		;I felt warm and cozy sitting by the fire.
	; -- (2) 
	; -- (3) (often disapproving) easy and convenient, but not always honest or right
		;The firm has a cozy relationship with the Department of Defense.
		;The danger is that things get too cozy.
	;;









